An edge bound shrinks a pinned view, and a zero intrinsic is not a size.

Two defects in the axis resolver, both found by following one vanished control from its rules to
the frame it was given. They are what made real constraints, arriving for the first time after
foundation 0087, place controls off the pane and at no size.

ONE. AN EDGE BOUND MOVES A VIEW ONLY WHILE ITS ORIGIN IS FREE. The resolver read:

  /* An edge bound moves the view rather than resizing it: the size is already settled. */
  if (axis->hasMaxFar && axis->origin + axis->size > axis->maxFar)
      axis->origin = axis->maxFar - axis->size;

which is right for an unpinned origin and wrong for a pinned one: it throws away the EQUALITY that
fixed the origin in order to satisfy an INEQUALITY, and the inequality is the weaker statement. A
label pinned leading to 205 with an intrinsic width of 914 inside a 600 wide container has a far
edge of 1119 against a maxFar of 600, so it was moved to 600 - 914 = -314. The Get Ready-Made
Shortcuts button went the same way and to the same x, which is the tell that one rule did both.

  NSButton     {205 145 189 24}  ->  {-314 145 176 23}   before
  NSButton     {205 145 189 24}  ->  { 205 145 176 23}   after
  NSTextField  {203  95 379 42}  ->  {-314  95 914 42}   before
  NSTextField  {203  95 379 42}  ->  { 205  95 395 42}   after, and 395 is 600 - 205

TWO. A ZERO INTRINSIC IS NOT A SIZE, it is a view that cannot answer yet. The fall through accepted
intrinsic >= 0, so a container whose intrinsic size comes from arranged subviews that have not been
laid out reported 0 and was resolved to nothing. The NSStackView holding iA Writer Light and Dark
radio buttons is pinned leading at 207 with a trailing bound of 580 and carries no size rule, so 0
won over its archived 182 and the radios were 0 points wide. Falling through to the current size
keeps what the archive or the last layout said, which is the conservative answer; a view that
genuinely wants no width says so with a constraint, and that path is above this one.

MEASURED ON THE WINDOW THAT FOUND THEM. iA Writer Preferences now draws its Light and Dark radios
with Light selected, its Get Ready-Made Shortcuts button correctly sized and placed, and BOTH
explanatory paragraphs complete and wrapped inside the pane where they were truncated before. That
is better than the window has rendered at any point, including before this series began.

STILL WRONG THERE, and not claimed as fixed: the Appearance and Dock icon labels still overlap, and
the two popups read Fade In slash dot dot dot. Those are the next thing.

Gates: dts 69 of 69, patch record PASS, roster sweep 7 of 7 CONTENT and roster input 7 of 7, byte
identical to the run before, with iA Writer looked at as the application that leans hardest on this
code.

